      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no definitive moral framework that universally justifies preemptive strikes as a standard foreign policy tool across all democratic countries. While just war theory might argue for self-defense or the prevention of unquantifiable harm, the lack of a secure \"human right to democratic stance\" makes such justifications highly contested and specific to the particular conflict at hand. Most serious political scientists emphasize that legal and ethical legitimacy for military intervention must be grounded in clear, proven threats and strict adherence to international law rather than a broad ideological obligation to protect democracy globally.",
